# 15. Security and Access Control

Implement role-based authorization for all pages, API calls, database operations, payment processing, and file access.

### Student permissions

Students may:
- Read and update their own permitted profile fields.
- View eligible rooms.
- Request an eligible room allocation.
- View their own bills and payments.
- Make payments for their own outstanding bills.
- Submit and view their own complaints.
- Read their own notifications.
- View permitted roommate details.

Students may not:
- Change their own role to administrator.
- Read another student's billing records.
- Modify another student's profile.
- Create or edit official bills.
- Mark their own payments as verified.
- Override room capacity.
- Modify administrator-only records.
- Access secret API credentials.

### Administrator permissions

Authorized administrators may:
- View and manage student records.
- Add rooms and maintain room inventory.
- Manage room allocations.
- Create and update bills.
- Record verified manual payments.
- Review online payment records.
- Manage complaints.
- Send SMS reminders.
- View operational reports.

Protect administrator operations with server-side authorization.

Use Firebase Security Rules and trusted backend functions. Do not leave the database in public read/write mode.

Keep a record of important administrative changes, including bill corrections, room reassignment, and payment adjustments.

