# 18. Implementation and Testing Instructions

Build the project in stages and verify each stage before moving to the next.

### Stage 1: Foundation
Create the React application, responsive layout, welcome page, navigation, and initial dashboard designs.

### Stage 2: Firebase setup
Connect Firebase Authentication, Firestore, and Storage. Configure the project and environment variables.

### Stage 3: Authentication and roles
Implement student registration/login, administrator registration/login, secure administrator-key validation, role-based redirects, and database security rules.

### Stage 4: Student profiles
Implement profile editing, photo uploads, mandatory-field validation, and profile persistence.

### Stage 5: Room management
Implement administrator room creation, block assignment, occupancy, and room availability.

### Stage 6: Room allocation
Implement academic-year restrictions, roommate details, confirmation dialogs, and transaction-safe allocation with a strict two-student limit.

### Stage 7: Bills
Implement administrator bill creation and the student-specific billing page.

### Stage 8: Payments
Implement manual payment recording, payment history, online gateway integration, secure verification, and receipts.

### Stage 9: Complaints
Implement complaint submission, photo attachments, administrator responses, and status tracking.

### Stage 10: SMS reminders
Configure the SMS provider, implement secure sending, store provider responses, and test actual delivery.

### Stage 11: Testing and deployment
Test the complete workflow, verify permissions, fix errors, and deploy the application.

Do not stop at generating the frontend. Continue until the backend, database, authentication, and required integrations are implemented or clearly identify any external configuration that remains necessary.

