# 19. Mandatory Acceptance Tests

Before declaring the application complete, verify the following:

1. A student can register, log in, and log out.
2. An administrator cannot register with an incorrect access key.
3. A student cannot access administrator pages or privileged backend functions.
4. A student must complete their profile before selecting a room.
5. First-year students see only Hemavati Block rooms.
6. Second- and third-year students see only Kaveri Block rooms.
7. Fourth-year students see only MCA Block rooms.
8. Administrators can create and edit room numbers.
9. A room can never contain more than two active student allocations.
10. Concurrent room-selection requests cannot overbook a room.
11. Students can view only their own bills and payment records.
12. Administrators can create separate room fee and mess fee bills.
13. Manual payments update balances correctly.
14. Online payments update balances only after trusted verification.
15. Failed or pending payments do not incorrectly mark bills as paid.
16. Students can submit complaints and see their statuses.
17. Administrators can update complaints and send responses.
18. Actual SMS reminders are sent only when the SMS provider is configured.
19. SMS delivery statuses reflect real provider responses.
20. Private records and secret keys cannot be accessed through the frontend or unauthorized API requests.
21. The application works on desktop and mobile screens.
22. All important data remains available after refreshing the browser or logging out and back in.

